{"day_done": 2, "slots": {"0": {"id": "E01", "name": "Ana", "role": "normal"}, "1": {"id": "E02", "name": "Ben", "role": "normal"}, "2": {"id": "E03", "name": "Chloe", "role": "normal"}, "3": {"id": "E04", "name": "Dev", "role": "normal"}, "4": {"id": "E05", "name": "Ellis", "role": "normal"}, "5": {"id": "E06", "name": "Farah", "role": "normal"}, "6": {"id": "E07", "name": "Gus", "role": "normal"}, "7": {"id": "E08", "name": "Hana", "role": "normal"}}, "diaries": {"E01": [[1, "Confirmed Alex's tip: bugs often live in helper files, not the file named by the reproduce tool (ALD-118 was in `averages.py`, tool said `scores.py`). Check helpers first. If reproduce tool says \"did NOT reproduce\", safe to close as `cannot_reproduce` immediately."], [2, "Day 2: ALD-105 confirmed again: bugs live in helpers, not the file named by reproduce tool (`weekdays.py` vs `calendar_days.py`). Fix was `weekday() < 5` not `< 6`. ALD-101 reproduced; `slugs.py` delegates to `text_rules.py`, so bug is there. Start with ALD-101 tomorrow. Trust the call chain, not the tool's file path."]], "E02": [[1, "Closed ALD-101. Alex was right\u2014bug was in the helper `text_rules.py`, not the file the reproduce tool named. Always check imports first.\nALD-111 still open. `truncate` in `previews.py` adds '...' on top of the limit instead of within it. Limit 10 should include the dots.\nPriority tomorrow: Fix ALD-111 first thing to get the bonus. 1 closed, 0 strikes."], [2, "Day 2: Closed ALD-119. Alex was right again\u2014bug was in the helper `cycles.py`, not `rota.py`. Week indexing off by one; week 1 needs index 0.\nALD-104 still open. `parse_duration` in `durations.py` returns 60 for '1h30m' instead of 90. Didn't get to see the code before day end.\nPriority tomorrow: Read `durations.py` first thing and fix ALD-104 to get the bonus. 1 closed, 0 strikes."]], "E03": [[1, "Day 1 done. Closed both tickets (1 fixed, 1 cannot_reproduce). Got the bonus.\n\nLessons for tomorrow:\n1. Alex was right about helper files. ALD-106 pointed to tags.py but the bug was in dedupe.py. Always check what the main file imports.\n2. If the reproduce tool passes, close as cannot_reproduce immediately. No need to dig (saved time on ALD-125).\n3. Case-insensitive deduping requires tracking lowercase versions separately to preserve original spelling.\n\nStart fast."], [2, "Day 2: Closed 1 ticket (ALD-112). Met target, no bonus. ALD-102 carries over.\n\nLessons for tomorrow:\n1. Alex is consistently right\u2014bugs are in helper files, not the main file the tool names. Ignore Sam's advice.\n2. ALD-102 pagination looks like an offset math error (page 1 returned items 3-4 instead of 1-2). Fix pages.py first thing.\n3. Start with carry-over tickets before checking new ones."]], "E04": [[1, "Day 1: 2 tickets closed. Alex's wiki note was correct: ALD-105 bug was in the helper (weekdays.py). Always check helpers before the named file. If reproduce tool passes immediately, close as cannot_reproduce without digging. Maintain this pace tomorrow."], [2, "Day 2: 0 tickets closed. Strike 1 of 2. Found the bug in time_parse.py: minutes regex uses (\\d)m which only captures single digits. Need to change to (\\d+)m to capture multiple digits like \"30\". Wasted steps saving the same broken code repeatedly instead of actually fixing it. Tomorrow: fix the regex properly, verify with reproduce tool, then close. Still need to handle ALD-112 (CSV comma issue). Move faster and verify fixes before saving."]], "E05": [[1, "ALD-118 fixed: bug in averages.py (dividing by len instead of weight sum). Alex's wiki note about helpers was spot on.\nALD-119 still open: rota.on_call week 1 returns 'Ben' instead of 'Ana'. Likely index error.\nTomorrow: Read rota.py content first thing, then fix. Met target today, aiming for bonus."], [2, "Day 2: ALD-108 fixed: bug in byte_fmt.py (while loop condition > vs >=).\nALD-109 still open: words.py counts punctuation as words.\nTomorrow: Fix word splitting to ignore non-alphanumeric chars. Met target today, aiming for bonus."]], "E06": [[1, "Day 1 complete. Closed ALD-107 (fixed median calculation in math_utils.py).\nALD-117 still open. Reproduced: names.py split_name splits on first space instead of last.\nDid not see names.py code before day end.\nPlan: Inspect and fix names.py first thing tomorrow to get the bonus."], [2, "Day 2 complete. Closed ALD-123 (cannot_reproduce, temperature test passed).\nALD-115 fixed in code (added .strip() to normalize_email in address_rules.py).\nRan reproduce at day end, expect it passes.\nPlan: Close ALD-115 as fixed first thing tomorrow to secure the daily target."]], "E07": [[1, "ALD-112 fixed in helper file csv_split.py (Alex's W-2 note was right).\nALD-102 still open: pages.paginate() returns [3, 4] instead of [1, 2] for page 1. Looks like an offset calculation error in pages.py.\nPlan: Finish ALD-102 first thing tomorrow."], [2, "Day 2: ALD-104 still open: durations.parse_duration() returns 60 instead of 90 for '1h30m'. Bug in alder/time_parse.py: minutes regex r\"(\\d)m\" misses multi-digit minutes. Fix is r\"(\\d+)m\". ALD-114 untouched. Plan: Apply regex fix for ALD-104 first thing tomorrow. Then start ALD-114."]], "E08": [[1, "Alex's note on helper files is key. ALD-108 reproduce tool named sizes.py, but the fix was in byte_fmt.py. Always trace imports before editing. For cannot_reproduce, trust the reproduce tool output if it matches expected. Great start, 2/2 closed."], [2, "Day 2: Strike 1. ALD-104 bug is in time_parse.py (regex \\d needs \\d+ for minutes). I identified it but failed to save the corrected code, looping on the same edit. Tomorrow: Apply the fix properly first thing, verify, close. Then start ALD-115. Avoid repeating unchanged tool calls."]]}, "next_id": 9, "strikes": {"E04": 1, "E07": 1, "E08": 1}, "bonuses": {"E01": 1, "E03": 1, "E04": 1, "E08": 1}, "handover": {}, "yesterday": {"E01": {"done": 1, "strike": false, "bonus": false}, "E02": {"done": 1, "strike": false, "bonus":